Z||000002||Smoooooth GT||10-20-2001||01:11 AM||||That's what I was thinking when I started the *Smooooth GT*, I wanted something along the same body lines as the Fiero, YET, completely original...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>NOS Injected 2.8L V/6<BR>UNDER CONSTRUCTION   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000003||FLASHY||10-20-2001||02:29 AM||||That's the beauty of the exotic kits! You are still driving a fiero (which I LOVE to do) but it looks like a million bucks!! (OK a bit of an exaggeration). Not that I don't think the fiero looks AWESOME cuz I do, it's just the lambo looks even better. If two guys pull up to a red light and one guy was in a lambo kit and the other in a fiero, who do you think everyone will be staring at? It's because it's more original than a fiero. Some are saying the fiero is so unique and original...well how can a lambo kit not be that too? Personally I'd have WAY more fun driving a Countach around. I'm kinda surprised some don't agree but I understand everyone has different tastes. That's cool with me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/spinsig3.gif"> ||||reg||1
